 "result": "the render thread falls by ~4 ms (Demo 12.0 -> 7.8, vs 13.9 -> 10.0) and the presenter costs ~5.0 ms (more than the ~3.4 ms the draw cost inline: hand-off and colder caches); but the main thread rises by 0.3-0.4 ms on every step (tick step and idle step ~+5-8%), which points to memory contention with the concurrent channel swap. The frame is bound by the slowest thread, which is main. Not committed (card: record and revert); the patch is parked at X5 logs/rtr2-presenter-parked.patch for when the main thread is below the render thread",
